% ipl_cert_defects_resolved (error): G(CertificationSignoff → ¬open_conformance_failure)
% Certification & Onboarding. Sign-off attests conformance to the model. A failing case is either a real counterparty defect or a model that does not match the ROE; either way it must be fixed and re-tested green, not signed over.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a CertificationSignoff
    and step the step has shown "open conformance failure"
then the policy ipl_cert_defects_resolved is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_drift_monitored (error): G(drift_detected → F(drift_resolved ∨ Incident))
% Digital Twin & Drift Detection. A certification is a snapshot; systems and specs change. Overlaying the IPL model's regions onto live sessions turns spec-vs-system divergence into an observable signal — but only if every detected drift is then driven to resolution or escalated, never silently ignored.
step a step meets "shows drift resolved or is a Incident" at a time if
    step the step has shown "drift resolved" at the time.

step a step meets "shows drift resolved or is a Incident" at a time if
    step the step was a Incident at the time.

step a step meets "it or a later step shows drift resolved or is a Incident" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step meets "shows drift resolved or is a Incident" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step has shown "drift detected"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step shows drift resolved or is a Incident"
then the policy ipl_cert_drift_monitored is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_invalid_flows_tested (error): (G(CertificationSignoff → P(invalid_flows_selected ∧ invalid_flows_tested))) ∧ G(VerificationResult → (produced_by(imandrax) ∨ oracle_type(imandrax))) ∧ G(StateSpaceAnalysisResult → (produced_by(imandrax) ∨ oracle_type(imandrax))) ∧ G(ConformanceResult → (produced_by(imandrax) ∨ oracle_type(imandrax))) ∧ G(CoSimulationResult → (produced_by(imandrax) ∨ oracle_type(imandrax)))
