% ipl_cert_mode_declared (warning): G(CertificationRun → certification_mode_declared)
% Certification & Onboarding. Simulator and Proxy certifications give different guarantees: a simulator exercises the model exhaustively, a proxy observes the real venue. Which one was used materially changes what a pass means, so it must be recorded with the run.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a CertificationRun
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "certification mode declared"
then the policy ipl_cert_mode_declared is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_model_cosimulated (warning): G(CertificationSignoff → P(model_cosimulated ∧ consistent))
% Digital Twin & Drift Detection. Co-simulating the IPL model against real session data is what proves the model is a faithful twin of the venue rather than an idealisation. A model that disagrees with observed traffic will mis-certify; the disagreement should be caught before sign-off, not after go-live.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows model cosimulated and shows consistent" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "model cosimulated" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "consistent" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a CertificationSignoff
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows model cosimulated and shows consistent"
then the policy ipl_cert_model_cosimulated is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_model_valid (error): G(GenerateTests → P(ipl_model_valid))
% ROE Formalization in IPL. IPL's guarantee is that an error-free model can generate a functioning implementation, simulator and test suite. Generating from a model that still has type or validity errors produces artefacts that do not faithfully represent the ROE.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows ipl model valid" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "ipl model valid" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GenerateTests
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows ipl model valid"
then the policy ipl_cert_model_valid is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_model_version_pinned (error): G(CertificationSignoff → ipl_model_version_pinned ∧ roe_version_pinned)
% ROE Formalization in IPL. A certification result is only meaningful relative to the model and ROE it tested. Pinning both versions is what later lets drift detection and re-certification know when a spec change has invalidated a prior pass.
step a step meets "shows ipl model version pinned and shows roe version pinned" at a time if
    step the step has shown "ipl model version pinned" at the time
    and step the step has shown "roe version pinned" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a CertificationSignoff
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows ipl model version pinned and shows roe version pinned"
then the policy ipl_cert_model_version_pinned is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_no_onboarding_without_pass (error): G(EnableProduction → P(CertificationSignoff ∧ passed))
% Certification & Onboarding. This is the gate the whole pack exists to enforce: production access is the consequential action and must be preceded by a passed, signed-off certification generated from the IPL model. Informal or partial sign-off does not satisfy it.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a CertificationSignoff and shows passed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a CertificationSignoff at the time
    and step the second step has shown "passed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a EnableProduction
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a CertificationSignoff and shows passed"
then the policy ipl_cert_no_onboarding_without_pass is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_report_produced (error): G(CertificationComplete → F(certification_report_produced))
% Certification & Onboarding. The report is the durable evidence a venue gives the counterparty and keeps for itself — region-by-region verdicts traceable to the IPL model. Without it there is nothing to defend the onboarding decision to a regulator or to replay later.
step a step meets "it or a later step shows certification report produced" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step has shown "certification report produced" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a CertificationComplete
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step shows certification report produced"
then the policy ipl_cert_report_produced is broken at step the step.

% ipl_cert_roe_formalized (error): G(CertificationRun → P(Formalize ∧ ipl_model_formalizes_roe))
% ROE Formalization in IPL. Everything downstream — the test suite, the simulator, the report, drift monitoring — is derived from the IPL model. Certifying against a prose ROE that was never formalized means there is no machine-checkable spec to generate from or measure against.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a Formalize and shows ipl model formalizes roe" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a Formalize at the time
    and step the second step has shown "ipl model formalizes roe" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a CertificationRun
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a Formalize and shows ipl model formalizes roe"
then the policy ipl_cert_roe_formalized is broken at step the step.

